# PROPRIETARY NVIDIA driver USE flags.
# Copied into the sysroot by build-x86-host-stage4.sh ONLY when NVIDIA_PROPRIETARY
# (--nvidia-driver proprietary). Headless / open-driver / Mesa-only images never
# reference these.
#
# kernel-open: build the open-source nvidia.ko kernel-interface variant (default
#   on modern Turing+/RTX hardware — the RTX 4060 on this fleet supports it). If
#   you must support pre-Turing (Maxwell/Pascal) GPUs, drop kernel-open to get the
#   legacy closed kernel module instead.
# persistenced / static-libs off: lean runtime; the proprietary userspace + the
#   X driver + the OpenGL/Vulkan libGLX_nvidia come with the package.
x11-drivers/nvidia-drivers kernel-open persistenced -static-libs
# NOTE: mesa has NO video_cards_nvidia flag (mesa is the open stack — nouveau).
# VIDEO_CARDS="… nvidia" (set in make.conf by the builder) makes x11-base/xorg-drivers
# pull x11-drivers/nvidia-drivers; the open Mesa stack stays co-installed for
# llvmpipe / non-NVIDIA GPUs. NVIDIA owns GLX/EGL/Vulkan ICDs at runtime via eselect.
#
# CUDA host compiler: the CLANG leg, NOT the gcc leg — the gcc leg is
# STRUCTURALLY UNSATISFIABLE in this builder. dev-util/nvidia-cuda-toolkit
# hard-caps its host compiler (nvidia-cuda-toolkit-12.9.2.ebuild: GCC_MAX_VER="14",
# CLANG_MAX_VER="19"):
#     RDEPEND="!clang? ( <sys-devel/gcc-15_pre[cxx] )
#              clang?  ( <llvm-core/clang-20_pre ) …"
# but the amd64 hardened stage3 seed already ships gcc 15 (seed
# stage3-amd64-hardened-openrc-20260719T170103Z: "gcc (Gentoo Hardened 15.3.0 p8)"),
# and build-x86-host-stage4.sh keeps the seed toolchain with a NAME-level
# `--exclude sys-devel/gcc` (EMERGE_EXCLUDE) — which masks EVERY installable
# gcc:14 candidate too, not just rebuilds of the seed slot. With the default
# USE=-clang the dep therefore had no candidate at all, dependency resolution
# aborted, and — resolution failure, so --keep-going could not help — NOT ONE
# payload package merged. Verbatim, from role edge_ai.x86 (out/sessions/
# 20260719-103006-a775c2/build-edge_ai.x86.log:153744):
#     !!! All ebuilds that could satisfy "<sys-devel/gcc-15_pre[cxx]" have been masked.
#     - sys-devel/gcc-14.3.1_p20260604::gentoo (masked by: exclude option)
#     (dependency required by "dev-util/nvidia-cuda-toolkit-12.9.2::gentoo[-clang]" [ebuild])
#     …
#     [build-x86] ERROR: stage4 payload incomplete — missing: grub-install dracut parted jq nmcli kubelet kubeadm containerd
# → the edge_ai x86 role emitted ZERO artifacts.
#
# USE=clang flips the toolkit onto its clang host-compiler leg, satisfied by
# llvm-core/clang-19.1.7-r1 — STABLE amd64 (KEYWORDS "…amd64…"), SLOT=19 (slotted,
# co-installable with any newer llvm/clang the payload pulls), and NOT touched by
# EMERGE_EXCLUDE (which excludes only sys-devel/gcc, sys-libs/glibc,
# sys-devel/binutils). The alternative — co-installing sys-devel/gcc:14 next to
# the seed — needs the builder to stop name-excluding gcc (an EMERGE_EXCLUDE
# change owned by build-x86-host-stage4.sh) and is a similarly large from-source
# build; the clang leg needs NO builder change. USE=clang changes nothing else in
# the ebuild but the dep leg + a pkg_setup version warning (nvidia-cuda-toolkit is
# a prepackaged-binary install; the host compiler is used AFTER boot, by nvcc).
# On the image, compile CUDA code with:  nvcc -ccbin clang++-19 …
# Guarded by scripts/preflight-cuda-host-compiler.sh (wired into
# tests/build-matrix/check.sh via tests/scripts/test-edge-ai-cuda-host-compiler.sh).
dev-util/nvidia-cuda-toolkit clang
